---
import { TextSection } from '@components/odyssey-theme';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Page.astro';

const seo = {
	title: 'Legal & Compliance | ATLAS Solutions',
	description: 'Privacy Policy, Terms of Service, and Compliance Statements for ATLAS cybersecurity auditing platform.',
};
---

<Layout {seo}>
	<TextSection narrow>
		<h1>Legal & Compliance</h1>
		<p class="legal-draft-notice">
			<strong>Draft Notice:</strong> These documents are provided as reference drafts and should be reviewed by qualified legal counsel before publication. Last updated: July 2026.
		</p>

		<!-- ============================================
		     PRIVACY POLICY
		     ============================================ -->
		<h2>Privacy Policy</h2>

		<h3>Information We Collect</h3>
		<p>
			ATLAS operates under a zero-retention model. During an audit engagement, our platform may temporarily access:
		</p>
		<ul class="legal-list">
			<li>SaaS application metadata (names, usage counts, license assignments)</li>
			<li>Cloud service inventory (AWS, Azure, GCP service accounts and roles)</li>
			<li>AI tool usage patterns (tool names, frequency of use — not content)</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			<strong>We do NOT collect, store, or transmit:</strong> employee PII, source code, financial records, customer data, passwords, API keys, or any proprietary business information.
		</p>

		<h3>Data Retention</h3>
		<p>
			All audit data is processed in ephemeral containers that self-destruct upon engagement completion. No raw data is retained on ATLAS servers, third-party cloud storage, or backup systems. Audit reports are delivered to you and may be stored at your discretion.
		</p>

		<h3>Data Processing Agreement</h3>
		<p>
			By engaging ATLAS services, you authorize us to process the limited metadata described above solely for the purpose of delivering audit findings. We act as a data processor under GDPR and do not determine the purposes or means of processing.
		</p>

		<!-- ============================================
		     TERMS OF SERVICE
		     ============================================ -->
		<h2>Terms of Service</h2>

		<h3>Engagement Model</h3>
		<p>
			ATLAS provides autonomous auditing services under a results-based pricing model. All engagements are backed by our Self-Funding Guarantee: if ATLAS does not uncover at least 3× our fee in recoverable waste, you pay nothing.
		</p>

		<h3>Limited Liability</h3>
		<p>
			While ATLAS employs enterprise-grade security measures, no automated system can guarantee absolute safety. By using our platform, you acknowledge that:
		</p>
		<ul class="legal-list">
			<li>Audit findings represent the best available intelligence at time of scan</li>
			<li>New vulnerabilities may emerge after audit completion</li>
			<li>ATLAS is not liable for third-party service outages or data breaches unrelated to our platform</li>
			<li>Liability is limited to the total fees paid by you during the 12 months preceding the claim</li>
		</ul>

		<h3>Intellectual Property</h3>
		<p>
			All audit reports, methodologies, and proprietary algorithms remain the intellectual property of ATLAS. You receive a perpetual, non-exclusive license to use audit findings for internal decision-making purposes only. Redistribution or resale of our methodology is prohibited.
		</p>

		<h3>Payment Terms</h3>
		<p>
			Invoices are due net 30 days from receipt. Late payments accrue interest at 1.5% per month or the maximum rate permitted by law, whichever is lower. ATLAS reserves the right to suspend services for overdue accounts.
		</p>

		<!-- ============================================
		     HIPAA COMPLIANCE STATEMENT
		     ============================================ -->
		<h2>HIPAA Compliance Statement</h2>
		<p>
			ATLAS audits are designed to be HIPAA-aware but do not constitute a covered entity or business associate relationship under the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act. Our platform does not process, store, or transmit protected health information (PHI). Healthcare organizations should consult their compliance officers regarding specific regulatory requirements.
		</p>

		<!-- ============================================
		     ZERO DATA LIABILITY POLICY
		     ============================================ -->
		<h2>Zero Data Liability Policy</h2>
		<p>
			ATLAS maintains a strict zero-data-liability posture:
		</p>
		<ul class="legal-list">
			<li>No raw audit data is retained beyond engagement completion</li>
			<li>No customer data is used for training, analytics, or third-party sharing</li>
			<li>All processing occurs within ephemeral, self-destructing containers</li>
			<li>Third-party cloud providers (AWS, Azure) are engaged under strict DPA terms that prohibit secondary use of customer data</li>
			<li>This policy is legally binding and enforceable. Violations result in immediate contract termination and potential liability for damages.</li>
		</ul>

		<!-- ============================================
		     CONTACT US
		     ============================================ -->
		<h2>Contact Us</h2>
		<p>For legal inquiries, data processing requests, or compliance questions:</p>
		<ul class="legal-list">
			<li><strong>Email:</strong> legal@atlas-solutions.com</li>
			<li><strong>Mail:</strong> ATLAS Solutions, 1234 Security Blvd, Suite 500, Austin, TX 78701</li>
			<li><strong>Response time:</strong> We respond to all legal inquiries within 2 business days</li>
		</ul>
	</TextSection>
</Layout>

<style>
	h2 {
		margin-top: 3rem;
		font-size: 1.75rem;
	}

	h3 {
		margin-top: 2rem;
		font-size: 1.25rem;
	}

	/* ============================================
	   LEGAL-SPECIFIC STYLING
	   ============================================ */
	.legal-draft-notice {
		background-color: var(--theme-surface-1);
		padding: 1.5rem;
		border-radius: var(--theme-shape-radius);
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
	}

	.legal-list {
		padding-left: 2rem;
		line-height: 1.8;
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}

	.legal-list li {
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
	}

	/* ============================================
	   RESPONSIVE
	   ============================================ */
	@media (max-width: 768px) {
		h2 {
			font-size: 1.5rem;
		}

		h3 {
			font-size: 1.1rem;
		}
	}
</style>
